++/*
++ * 0199: PM6150 charger (SMB5) input-current setup.
++ *
++ * Observed (0195b, logs/boot-0195b.txt): on USB at 14 %, "SWEET BATTERY: ... -122mA external=1
++ * charging=1": the charger is in fast charge but the battery still drains about 100 mA, so the
++ * input current limit is below the phone's load (the USER: "battery drained even though
++ * connected"). Nothing in this kernel ever configured the charger; it runs with what XBL/ABL left.
++ *
++ * Register map and the input-current-limit sequence are Xiaomi's own sweet kernel
++ * (MiCode/Xiaomi_Kernel_OpenSource sweet-r-oss, drivers/power/supply/qcom/smb5-reg.h, smb5-lib.c
++ * smblib_set_icl_current/smblib_icl_override, qpnp-smb5.c pm6150 charge params): SID 0, CHGR 0x1000,
++ * DCDC 0x1100, BATIF 0x1200, USBIN 0x1300, TYPEC 0x1500, MISC 0x1600; ICL 0x1370 and FCC 0x1061 in
++ * 50 mA steps. The sunfish port's read-only dump of the same PMIC (ios-flame
++ * docs/reference/charger-regs.md) showed XBL leaving FCC 2.0 A / ICL 1.5 A there.
++ *
++ *   sweetcharge=1  read only: one register dump (CHGR/DCDC/BATIF/USBIN/TYPEC/MISC) at start and after
++ *                  each plug-in, a status line on every change and every 60 s
++ *   sweetcharge=2  ... and the input current limit set from the detected source, as smblib does in
++ *                  high-current mode (USBIN_MODE_CHG=1, no ICL override, ICL kept after APSD):
++ *                    Type-C Rp 3.0 A: 2000 mA, Rp 1.5 A: 1500 mA, DCP/QC: 1500 mA, CDP: 1500 mA,
++ *                    float/other: 1000 mA, SDP (a PC port): sweetchgsdp (default 500 = left alone;
++ *                    900 or 1500 only if the charger's AICL is enabled, which backs off on a weak port);
++ *                    capped at sweetchgmax (default 2000, at most 3000). A target of 500 mA or less is
++ *                    never written. FCC (battery charge current) is raised to 2000 mA only if it is
++ *                    lower (0.4 C for the 5020 mAh cell). USB input suspend is cleared, charging enable
++ *                    set when the charger says disabled, the charger watchdog petted when it is enabled.
++ *                  Float voltage, JEITA, termination and safety timers are never written.
++ * Every write is to a fixed whitelist (bsd/dev/sweet_spmi.c sweet_spmi_write), read back and logged.
++ */
